# Normalize every text file to LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a default Windows clone materializes text files with CRLF, which breaks the
# shipped shell scripts outright (bash chokes on \r) and diverges byte-for-byte from the content
# every fingerprint/guard compares against. All blobs are already LF-normalized in the index
# (git's text=auto detection), so this changes nothing on macOS/Linux and only affects what a
# Windows checkout writes to disk. Binary formats stay protected by git's auto detection.
* text=auto eol=lf
